text: >-
  That is, the search warrant seems to know nothing about the personal surrender
  note to Lance

  himself, only the post written for everyone (and which contains the word "all"
  five times!). Our

  view is that the "Zealous Monkey" post was indeed created contemporaneously,
  at 7:57 pm, but

  that the "indictment" surrender must have been fabricated after 1 am the next
  day. It's

  interesting that only here do we have any notion that the sheriff friend (Mike
  Mitchell) was a

  (former) deputy, indeed, as far as we were able to ascertain, that piece of
  information (that the

  facilitator was a deputy) had never been placed in the public domain prior to
  the 15th (with the

  indictment), and that it was indeed Mitchell, confirmed by the search
  warrants, was only

  revealed by Candace Owens around the 17th or so. To underline this point, the
  PCA knows

  nothing about any deputy.
